<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baldwin Spencer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Winston Baldwin Spencer</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baldwin Spencer is an Antiguan politician and former trade unionist who led the United Progressive Party and was prime minister of Antigua and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbuda">Barbuda</a> from 2004 to 2014. His victory in 2004 ended nearly three decades of rule by the Bird family's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigua-labour-party">Antigua Labour Party</a>. His government faced the collapse of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allen-stanford">Allen Stanford</a>'s financial empire in 2009.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baldwin-spencer.jpg" alt="Baldwin Spencer" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fernanda LeMarie - Cancillería del Ecuador · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BaldwinSpencer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
